-- What the property runner draws an argument from: `draw(seed, size)` yields one value of the type and the seed that follows it, the value no larger than `size` admits, so a run that grows its size meets small counterexamples first.
--
-- Each carrier's witness lives in the module that owns the carrier, beside that module's `Spell`, and the positional tuple shapes are in `/std/Tuple`. Every carrier `Spell` renders is drawn but `Flt`, whose distribution — the non-finite values included — is a decision nobody has taken; the tuple shapes are drawn through arity 3, the shapes `Spell` renders.
use /std/{Nat};
use /std/Test/{Seed};

pub concept Draw(A: Type): pub Type {
    draw(Seed, Nat) -> {A, Seed},
}

pub use Draw/*;
